    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the elite 76.14 score of **Yordan Alvarez**. Despite a modest park factor, his elite xwOBA of 0.424 against Brandon Sproat makes him our primary anchor. We are also leaning heavily into the speed-to-base potential of **Trea Turner** (74.93) and **Kyle Schwarber** (74.24), both of whom benefit significantly from facing Roki Sasaki. While Sasaki is a high-profile arm, his 5.11 xERA suggests vulnerability; **Trea Turner** in particular is positioned to capitalize on the high-contact upside against a pitcher who has struggled with command. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.83) rounds out our top-tier plays, offering a massive 14% platoon boost that solidifies his role at the top of the order against Kyle Leahy.\n\nStrategic platoon advantages are driving much of our middle-tier value, most notably for **Christian Yelich**, who draws a 68.25 score against Peter Lambert, and **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30), who benefits from a 16% park factor uplift. **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) warrants special attention today; while his raw projections are modest, the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and the likelihood of stealing bases against Ryan Feltner\u2014who displays a slow delivery\u2014makes him a sneaky high-ceiling start. On the bubble, **Chase Meidroth** was our toughest omission; his 49.99 score narrowly missed the cut, ultimately squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-scoring outfielders and our commitment to maintaining daily efficiency. We are monitoring **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith** closely; while their scores are solid, their status remains \"Lineup Pending.\" Should either fall out of the top two spots in their respective orders, their efficiency scores will crater, necessitating a pivot to our bench depth.",
